WOW-BG3 benilla patch 0055: the fight's own narration stays out of WoW's chat.

- wowbg3_fight.rs: the bridge's fight log ("Turn 4: your turn", "a Young Wolf joins the fight",
  "Fight over: victory") and benilla's own fight lines ("N mobs pulled into a BG3 fight", "N more
  joining the BG3 fight", "BG3 started a fight with N mob(s)") were printed into WoW's chat as
  "[BG3] ..." system lines. BG3's own turn order and combat banners already say all of it, so the
  lines now go to benilla's log only (`info!("wowbg3 fight: ...")`, the same text `say` writes) and
  WoW's chat keeps WoW's own messages. The read cursor `f.printed` still advances line by line, so
  nothing is replayed when the switch is turned back on mid-fight.
- New `narrate()` beside `say()`, and `fight_chat_in_wow()`, read once per process.
- Kill switch: `WOW_BG3_FIGHT_CHAT=show` in BG3's environment prints them in WoW's chat again,
  exactly as before.
- WOW-BG3's own messages to the player (a refused pull, "Not your turn", the bridge not answering)
  are untouched; the per-turn help line was already off in world mode.

